WEBVTT

00:00:00.427 --> 00:00:08.090
In this video, you will change your contest after you have created it: the dates, the name, the message, the prize, and the rules.

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:10.953
Plans change, and the site is built for that.

00:00:10.953 --> 00:00:12.078
We start on the map.

00:00:12.924 --> 00:00:14.598
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:17.516 --> 00:00:20.066
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:21.724 --> 00:00:22.704
Then tap Allow.

00:00:26.364 --> 00:00:29.572
Now look at the top of the map, beside the search box.

00:00:29.572 --> 00:00:32.354
See your picture, or your initial, in a circle?

00:00:32.354 --> 00:00:36.917
That is your account menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:36.917 --> 00:00:37.618
Tap it.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:42.189
In the menu, tap Your contests.

00:00:44.814 --> 00:00:48.910
That is where the contests you run, and the homes you entered, live.

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:49.767
Tap Mine.

00:00:51.559 --> 00:00:53.529
This is your personal page.

00:00:53.529 --> 00:00:58.996
It lists the contests you run, if you run any, and the homes you entered, with their status.

00:00:58.996 --> 00:01:01.105
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:01:02.837 --> 00:01:06.938
This opens your dashboard, the control room for your contest.

00:01:06.938 --> 00:01:11.852
Plans change, and you can change your contest at any time before you announce winners.

00:01:11.852 --> 00:01:17.318
On the Overview, find Schedule, which shows when entries close and when voting runs.

00:01:17.318 --> 00:01:18.560
Tap Change dates.

00:01:20.221 --> 00:01:23.540
That opens the Details tab, where you edit your contest.

00:01:24.365 --> 00:01:29.774
Here you can move the day entries close, the day voting starts, and the day voting ends.

00:01:29.774 --> 00:01:33.857
Voting should start after entries close, and end after it starts.

00:01:33.857 --> 00:01:37.671
If you need more time for neighbors to enter, move these dates later.

00:01:38.513 --> 00:01:45.390
Scroll down and you can also change the contest name, the welcome message, the prize, and the official rules.

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:47.473
Neighbors see the changes right away.

00:01:48.332 --> 00:01:50.522
When you are done, tap Save changes.

00:01:52.192 --> 00:01:59.405
Everyone on your team is emailed about the change, so nobody is surprised, and you have a record of what changed.

00:01:59.405 --> 00:02:03.227
Only the person who created the contest can make these changes.

00:02:04.065 --> 00:02:07.271
One more card is on this tab: Run it again.

00:02:07.271 --> 00:02:15.506
Next year, it starts a new contest with the same rules, categories, prizes, sponsors and judges, and every date a year later.

00:02:15.506 --> 00:02:19.309
You tap twice to confirm, and you can edit it before it opens.

00:02:19.309 --> 00:02:21.151
A new contest may need a pass.

00:02:22.115 --> 00:02:23.628
Next up: Run voting.
